Supersedes #988, whose shared head branch was concurrently rewritten after review fixes were applied.

## Roadmap ownership

- Owning case: #957 / A1.3
- Builds on direct semantic family operations merged in #986
- H1 consumers: #958 / A2 and #61 / A3

## What changed

Add recursive scene-facing add/remove semantics on the authoritative `SemanticStore`:

- `add_semantic_scene_nodes(ids)` validates the full batch, collapses descendant roots already represented in the scene projection, promotes unaffected branches in place, then appends explicit target nodes in caller order;
- `remove_semantic_scene_nodes(ids)` removes explicit targets while dissolving only affected family roots and promoting surviving branches at the former root position;
- family membership, source identity, semantic identity, and authored state are not mutated;
- a crate-private root-splice primitive performs bounded local writes to the replaced root, replacement nodes, and immediate neighbors;
- the new module is actually compiled through ordinary Rust module ownership.

## Review fixes

The prototype sorted affected roots by `SemanticNodeId` before cross-root alias de-duplication. That is incorrect after detach/re-attach because NodeId allocation order can disagree with authored scene order. This version uses current linked scene-root order whenever multiple affected roots require first-occurrence de-duplication; the common single-root case avoids the scan.

## Tests

Focused tests cover:
- adding a family collapses existing descendant roots and appends the family;
- removing a descendant promotes a surviving sibling at the exact family-root position;
- invalid mixed batches fail before scene membership changes;
- cross-root alias de-dup follows authored scene order even when NodeId order intentionally disagrees after detach/re-attach.

## Architecture

- one `SemanticStore` / `SemanticNodeId` authority;
- no duplicate family graph, root-order cache, frontend model, runtime model, codec, or renderer dependency;
- no new `#[path]`/`include!` debt;
- reparent/reorder and transform/style mutations remain for the atomic mutation vocabulary rather than ad-hoc partial transactions here.

Refs #953 #957 #958 #61 #961.

Fixes the trusted Cloudflare delivery first-use path after PR #441 reached exact-head green gates but preview delivery failed because `wrangler versions upload` cannot create a Worker.

Root cause observed in trusted delivery run `33712652941`:
- authorization succeeded;
- exact-SHA gate succeeded;
- artifact identity validation succeeded;
- `wrangler versions upload` failed with: `You cannot upload a new version of a Worker that does not yet exist. Please run the deploy command first.`

Fix:
- keep the normal path as `wrangler versions upload --preview-alias`;
- only when Wrangler returns that exact first-use error, create the Worker with a trusted inert 503 bootstrap Worker;
- bootstrap config contains only Worker name, compatibility date, `workers_dev`, and `preview_urls` — no routes, assets, or PR code;
- retry the non-active exact PR version upload after bootstrap;
- fail closed for every other upload failure;
- record whether first-use bootstrap occurred in delivery evidence.

Security boundary remains unchanged: Cloudflare credentials are only mapped in the trusted workflow on `main`; no PR/source package scripts execute while the token is present. The development Custom Domain is not deployed by this preview path.

## Stacked Batch 2 hardening

This PR is intentionally stacked on **#28 / `hardening/compatibility-architecture-v5`** because live GitHub state shows Batch 1 is still an open draft rather than merged into `main`. It must not be merged independently of #28.

### Objective

Generalise physical/device qualification and bind every release candidate to reproducible runtime/provenance evidence without broadening OTAST's mutation boundary. Magisk/Zygisk Next/Vector/IHI remain observational unless already covered by an explicit managed-target contract.

### Implemented so far

- canonical `otast-runtime-v1` digest over exact shipping `module/` paths, normalized modes and bytes; generated `release.properties` is provenance-only and excluded from the runtime digest;
- sanitized physical qualification registry with the existing Pixel 9a v1.0.3 proof represented as legacy/stale runtime-unbound evidence, not current qualification;
- qualification-registry validation and root-exposure attribution semantics (`PASS`, `PASS_WITH_ATTRIBUTION`, `FAIL`, `INCONCLUSIVE`);
- release bundle schema v2 binding source SHA, runtime digest, ZIP SHA, compatibility registry hash and qualification registry hash;
- deterministic repository gate now validates qualification metadata and runtime digest reproducibility.

### Still in progress

- finish Batch-1 prerequisite CI repairs carried by the stacked base;
- registry-driven device collector and physical proof producer/validator;
- runtime-equivalent proof reuse contract;
- upgrade-path fake-root qualification;
- fresh release target/dependency monitor integration;
- daily target-monitor cadence and semantic review improvements;
- exact Actions SHA pinning + update path;
- documentation and governance recommendations;
- complete CI/fake-root/build/ZIP/release-state review.

Do **not** merge or publish v1.0.3 from this draft. Issue #16 remains the physical acceptance gate.

